Package: tuxsitter
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, nftables, polkitd | policykit-1, systemd
Recommends: gir1.2-xapp-1.0 | gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1, gir1.2-notify-0.7
Maintainer: chpusch <chpusch@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/chpusch/tuxsitter
Description: Simple parental controls for Linux desktops
 Tuxsitter limits screen time per day (school days, weekend, holidays),
 restricts usage to allowed hours, lets parents grant extra time with a PIN
 and filters the internet for children's accounts only via a per-account
 DNS filter (Cloudflare Family, CleanBrowsing, AdGuard Family, OpenDNS,
 NextDNS profile or a custom server) with SafeSearch, YouTube Restricted
 Mode and blocking of DNS-over-HTTPS workarounds.
 .
 Made for Linux Mint (Cinnamon); works on other Ubuntu/Debian based desktops.
